From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Mower <mdmower@cmphys.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:50:42 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [bugs #2893] Warn about an empty translation unit only when
 it is empty

The rule for an empty file in SDCC.y is the default reduction of the
first parser state. The parser reduces by it for every first token that
cannot begin an external declaration, and reports the syntax error for
that token afterwards. The action of the rule gave warning 190, "ISO C
forbids an empty translation unit", without a condition. Files that
start with ';' or '}' got this warning before their syntax error.

The action now gives the warning only when the lookahead token is the
end of the input. Translation units that do not have a token still get
it.

Adds support/valdiag/tests/bug-2893.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/SDCC.y                       |  4 +++-
 support/valdiag/tests/bug-2893.c | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 support/valdiag/tests/bug-2893.c

diff --git a/src/SDCC.y b/src/SDCC.y
index 95b6cc650..b91962c44 100644
--- a/src/SDCC.y
+++ b/src/SDCC.y
@@ -2708,7 +2708,9 @@ function_body
 file
    : /* empty */
      {
-       werror(W_EMPTY_TRANSLATION_UNIT);
+       /* The parser also reduces by this rule when the first token cannot begin a translation unit, and it reports the syntax error afterwards. */
+       if (yychar == YYEOF)
+         werror(W_EMPTY_TRANSLATION_UNIT);
      }
    | translation_unit
    ;
diff --git a/support/valdiag/tests/bug-2893.c b/support/valdiag/tests/bug-2893.c
new file mode 100644
index 000000000..54bc6e6ea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/support/valdiag/tests/bug-2893.c
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+/* bug-2893.c
+
+   A first token that cannot begin a translation unit is a syntax error, and
+   it does not get the warning for an empty translation unit.
+ */
+
+#ifdef TEST1
+; /* ERROR(SDCC) */ /* WARNING(GCC) */
+int a;
+#endif
+
+#ifdef TEST2
+} /* ERROR */
+int b;
+#endif
+
+#ifdef TEST3
+/* valdiag.py does not report additional messages for lines that are marked,
+   so this line is not marked for SDCC. valdiag.py ignores messages that
+   contain the text of this token. The syntax error is such a message, and
+   the warning for an empty translation unit is not. */
+'unreferenced function argument' /* IGNORE(GCC) */
+#endif
+
+#ifdef TEST4
+/* A translation unit of comments and directives gets the warning. SDCC gives
+   it for the line after the pragma, which is the last line that the
+   preprocessor passes to the compiler. */
+#ifdef __SDCC
+#pragma std_c99
+#else /* WARNING(SDCC) */
+int c;
+#endif
+#endif
